  "response": "**Setup (Bayes' theorem):**\n\n- Prevalence: P(D) = 1/500 = 0.002, P(¬D) = 0.998\n- Sensitivity: P(+|D) = 0.98\n- Specificity: P(–|¬D) = 0.95 → P(+|¬D) = 0.05\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nP(+) = P(+|D)P(D) + P(+|¬D)P(¬D)\nP(+) = (0.98 × 0.002) + (0.05 × 0.998)\nP(+) = 0.00196 + 0.0499 = 0.05186\n\nP(D|+) = P(+|D)P(D) / P(+) = 0.00196 / 0.05186 ≈ 0.037794\n\nConverting to a percentage: **3.7794%** → rounds to **3.78%**\n\nThis illustrates the classic base-rate effect: even with a fairly sensitive and specific test, because the condition is rare, most positive results are false positives.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 3.78",
